Derivation -- Derivation defined on a noncommutative algebra
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        delta = derivation(A,output,sigma)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note free algebra: FreeAlgebra,, or a *note FreeAlgebraQuotient:
        FreeAlgebra / Ideal,.
      * output, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * sigma, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * delta, an instance of the type *note Derivation: Derivation,, 

Description
===========

This function returns a Derivation object, which may be used to perform
computations with (twisted) derivations in a noncommutative algebra.  A linear
map $\delta : A \to A$ is called a $\sigma$-derivation provided for all $x,y
\in A$, one has $\delta(xy) = \delta(x)y + \sigma(x)\delta(y)$. Such maps are
useful in defining many noncommutative algebras, including Ore extensions.

Below we give a simple example of a twisted derivation that is used to define
the subalgebras appearing in Fomin and Procesi's work to describe
Fomin-Kirillov algebras.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ<|x,y|>                                 |
|                                                   |
|o1 = A                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : FreeAlgebra                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : sigma = map(A,A,{y,x})                        |
|                                                   |
|o2 = map (A, A, {y, x})                            |
|                                                   |
|o2 : RingMap A <-- A                               |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : delta = derivation(A,{-x*y,y*x},sigma)        |
|                                                   |
|o3 = Derivation{generators => HashTable{x => -x*y}}|
|                                        y => y*x   |
|                homomorphism => map (A, A, {y, x}) |
|                "imageCache" => MutableHashTable{} |
|                matrix => | -xy yx |               |
|                source => A                        |
|                                                   |
|o3 : Derivation                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : delta y^2                                     |
|                                                   |
|o4 = x*y*x + y*x*y                                 |
|                                                   |
|o4 : A                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+

Methods that use an object of class Derivation:
===============================================

  * "Derivation RingElement"
  * "Derivation ZZ"
  * "oreExtension(Ring,RingMap,Derivation,RingElement)" -- see *note
    oreExtension: oreExtension, -- Creates an Ore extension of a noncommutative
    ring
  * "oreExtension(Ring,RingMap,Derivation,Symbol)" -- see *note oreExtension:
    oreExtension, -- Creates an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring
  * "oreIdeal(Ring,RingMap,Derivation,RingElement)" -- see *note oreIdeal:
    oreIdeal, -- Creates the defining ideal of an Ore extension of a
    noncommutative ring
  * "oreIdeal(Ring,RingMap,Derivation,Symbol)" -- see *note oreIdeal: oreIdeal,
    -- Creates the defining ideal of an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Derivation: Derivation, is a *note type: (Macaulay2Doc)Type,,
with ancestor classes *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, < *note Thing:
(Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in AssociativeAlgebras/doc.m2:1692:0.

