===========

This function creates a free algebra over $R$ with variables from the BasicList
xs.  Options are also passed as part of the BasicList. The variables are not in
scope after a call to this function by default. If you wish to have them in
scope, one may *note use: (Macaulay2Doc)use, the return value, or pass the
option true to UseVariables.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : A = freeAlgebra(QQ,{x,y,z})|
|                                |
|o1 = A                          |
|                                |
|o1 : FreeAlgebra                |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : use A                      |
|                                |
|o2 = A                          |
|                                |
|o2 : FreeAlgebra                |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : assert(x == A_0)           |
+--------------------------------+

Other options are *note Degrees: (Macaulay2Doc)Degrees,, *note DegreeRank:
(Macaulay2Doc)DegreeRank,, *note Weights: (Macaulay2Doc)Weights,, and *note
Heft: (Macaulay2Doc)Heft, which use the same syntax and play the same role as
in the case of a commutative polynomial ring.

In particular, to create noncommutative elimination orders, one must use *note
Weights: (Macaulay2Doc)Weights, that are chosen accordingly.  The following
example is the graph ideal of the ring homomorphism from $\mathbb{Q}\langle
a,b,c\rangle$ to $\mathbb{Q}\langle x,y\rangle$ satisfying $a \mapsto xyx$, $b
\mapsto yxy$ and $c \mapsto xy$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : B = freeAlgebra(QQ,{x,y,a,b,c,Weights=>{1,1,0,0,0},Degrees=>{1,1,3,3,2  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = B                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : FreeAlgebra                                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|}})                                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I = ideal {a - x*y*x, b - y*x*y, c - x*y}                               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = ideal (- x*y*x + a, - y*x*y + b, - x*y + c)                             |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Ideal of B                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Igb = NCGB(I,10)                                                        |
|Warning:  F4 Algorithm not available over current coefficient ring or        |
|Converting to Naive algorithm.                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = | xy-c cx-a yc-b ay-c2 ya-bx xb-c2 c3-ab abx-c2a abc-cab |              |
|                                                                             |
|             1      9                                                        |
|o6 : Matrix B  <-- B                                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|inhomogeneous ideal.                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This general construction is automated in *note ncGraphIdeal: ncGraphIdeal, and
*note ncKernel: ncKernel,.

