ncBasis -- Returns a basis of an noncommutative ring in specified degrees.
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        bas = ncBasis(d,e,B)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, or *note List:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List, or *note InfiniteNumber:
        (Macaulay2Doc)InfiniteNumber,
      * e, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, or *note List:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List, or *note InfiniteNumber:
        (Macaulay2Doc)InfiniteNumber,
      * B, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Limit => ..., default value infinity
      * Strategy => ..., default value "F4Parallel"
  * Outputs:
      * bas, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 

Description
===========

This command returns a basis (or minimal generating set, if the ground ring is
not a field), of a graded noncommutative ring.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ<|x,y,z|>                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = A                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : FreeAlgebra                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : p = y*z + z*y - x^2                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|        2                                                                    |
|o2 = - x  + y*z + z*y                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : A                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : q = x*z + z*x - y^2                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|            2                                                                |
|o3 = x*z - y  + z*x                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : A                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : r = z^2 - x*y - y*x                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|                    2                                                        |
|o4 = - x*y - y*x + z                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : A                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I = ideal{p,q,r}                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|               2                     2                       2               |
|o5 = ideal (- x  + y*z + z*y, x*z - y  + z*x, - x*y - y*x + z )              |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Ideal of A                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : B = A/I                                                                 |
|Warning:  F4 Algorithm not available over current coefficient ring or        |
|Converting to Naive algorithm.                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = B                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : FreeAlgebraQuotient                                                     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|inhomogeneous ideal.                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : bas = ncBasis(4,B)                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = | y3x y4 yzyx yzy2 yzyz zy2x zy3 zyzx zyzy z2yx z2y2 z2yz z3x z3y z4 |  |
|                                                                             |
|             1      15                                                       |
|o7 : Matrix B  <-- B                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

