ncKernel -- Compute the graph ideal of a ring map between noncommutative rings.
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        I = ncKernel f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * DegreeLimit => ..., default value 10
      * Strategy => ..., default value "F4"
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 

Description
===========

This function computes (a Groebner basis of) the kernel of a ring map between
noncommutative rings.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ<|a,b,c|>                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = A                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : FreeAlgebra                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : B = QQ<|x,y|>                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = B                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : FreeAlgebra                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(B,A,{x*y*x,y*x*y,x*y})                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = map (B, A, {x*y*x, y*x*y, x*y})                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : RingMap B <-- A                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : K = ncKernel f                                                          |
|Warning:  F4 Algorithm not available over current coefficient ring or        |
|Converting to Naive algorithm.                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = ideal 0                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of A                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|inhomogeneous ideal.                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The generators returned by this function are in fact a Groebner basis of the
kernel, so it may not be a minimal generating set.

The *note DegreeLimit: (Macaulay2Doc)DegreeLimit, and *note Strategy:
(Macaulay2Doc)Strategy, options are forwarded on to the call to the Groebner
basis routine *note NCGB: NCGB,.

