normalElements(RingMap,ZZ) -- Finds elements normalized by a ring map
*********************************************************************

  * Function: *note normalElements: normalElements,
  * Usage: 
        normalElements(f,n)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a homogeneous degree in which
        to search for normal elements
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 

Description
===========

A normal element x in a non-commutative ring R determines an automorphism f of
R by a*x=x*f(a). Conversely, given a ring endomorphism, we may ask if any x
satisfy the above equation for all a.

Given a ring map f and a degree n, this method returns solutions to the
equations a*x=x*f(a) for all generators a of R.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = skewPolynomialRing(QQ,(-1)_QQ,{x,y,z,w})                            |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = B                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : FreeAlgebraQuotient                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : sigma = map(B,B,{y,z,w,x})                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = map (B, B, {y, z, w, x})                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : RingMap B <-- B                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = oreExtension(B,sigma,a)                                             |
|Warning:  F4 Algorithm not available over current coefficient ring or        |
|Converting to Naive algorithm.                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = C                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : FreeAlgebraQuotient                                                     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|inhomogeneous ideal.                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : sigmaC = map(C,C,{y,z,w,x,a})                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = map (C, C, {y, z, w, x, a})                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : RingMap C <-- C                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : normalElements(sigmaC,1)                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = | a |                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|             1      1                                                        |
|o5 : Matrix C  <-- C                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : normalElements(sigmaC,2)                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = 0                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|              1                                                              |
|o6 : Matrix QQ  <-- 0                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : normalElements(sigmaC * sigmaC,2)                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = | a2 |                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|             1      1                                                        |
|o7 : Matrix C  <-- C                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : normalElements(sigmaC * sigmaC * sigmaC, 3)                             |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = | a3 |                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|             1      1                                                        |
|o8 : Matrix C  <-- C                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

