oppositeRing -- Creates the opposite ring of a noncommutative ring
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Aop = oppositeRing A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note quotient of a free algebra: FreeAlgebra / Ideal,, or *note
        FreeAlgebra: FreeAlgebra,
  * Outputs:
      * Aop, a *note quotient of a free algebra: FreeAlgebra / Ideal,, or *note
        FreeAlgebra: FreeAlgebra,

Description
===========

Given a noncommutative ring A, this creates a noncommutative ring whose
defining ideal is generated by the "opposites" - elements whose noncommutative
monomial terms have been reversed - of the generators of the defining ideal of
A.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[q]/ideal{q^4+q^3+q^2+q+1}                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = skewPolynomialRing(R,q,{x,y,z,w})                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = A                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : FreeAlgebraQuotient                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : x*y == q*y*x                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Aop = oppositeRing A                                                    |
|Warning:  F4 Algorithm not available over current coefficient ring or        |
|Converting to Naive algorithm.                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = Aop                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : FreeAlgebraQuotient                                                     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|inhomogeneous ideal.                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : y*x == q*x*y                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note skewPolynomialRing: skewPolynomialRing, -- Defines a skew polynomial
    ring via a skewing matrix

