oreExtension -- Creates an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        oreExtension(A,sigma,delta,x) or oreExtension(A,sigma,x)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * sigma, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, 
      * delta, an instance of the type *note Derivation: Derivation,, 
      * x, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, or a *note Symbol:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Degree => ..., default value 1
  * Outputs:
      * a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, 

Description
===========

This method calls *note oreIdeal: oreIdeal, and returns the associated Ore
extension as an FreeAlgebraQuotient.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = skewPolynomialRing(QQ,(-1)_QQ,{x,y,z,w})                            |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = B                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : FreeAlgebraQuotient                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : sigma = map(B,B,{y,z,w,x})                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = map (B, B, {y, z, w, x})                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : RingMap B <-- B                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = oreExtension(B,sigma,a)                                             |
|Warning:  F4 Algorithm not available over current coefficient ring or        |
|Converting to Naive algorithm.                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = C                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : FreeAlgebraQuotient                                                     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|inhomogeneous ideal.                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

One may define the Weyl algebra as an Ore extension using the identity
endomorphism and the usual polynomial derivative as the derivation.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : B = toFreeAlgebraQuotient(QQ[x])                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = B                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : FreeAlgebra                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : sigma = map(B,B,{x})                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = map (B, B, {x})                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : RingMap B <-- B                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : delta = derivation(B,{1_B})                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = Derivation{generators => HashTable{x => 1}   }                          |
|                homomorphism => map (B, B, {x})                              |
|                "imageCache" => MutableHashTable{}                           |
|                matrix => | 1 |                                              |
|                source => B                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Derivation                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : C = oreExtension(B,sigma,delta,dx)                                      |
|Warning:  F4 Algorithm not available over current coefficient ring or        |
|Converting to Naive algorithm.                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = C                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : FreeAlgebraQuotient                                                     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|inhomogeneous ideal.                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Of course, if one wants to perform extensive calculations with classical Weyl
Algebras, one should use the *note WeylAlgebra:
(Macaulay2Doc)monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmWeylAlgebra=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, option when
creating a polynomial ring.

In order to get the most out of the AssociativeAlgebras package, rings often
need to be graded.  To obtain such a ring from this construction, the
derivation must increase the degree by one.

See also
========

  * *note oreIdeal: oreIdeal, -- Creates the defining ideal of an Ore extension
    of a noncommutative ring

