toCommRing -- Compute the abelianization of a Ring and returns a Ring.
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        S = toCommRing R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note quotient of a free algebra: FreeAlgebra / Ideal,, or *note
        FreeAlgebra: FreeAlgebra,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * SkewCommutative => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false
  * Outputs:
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 

Description
===========

This method takes a noncommutative ring and returns the quotient of a
commutative polynomial ring (or an exterior algebra, if SkewCommutative=>true)
on the same generators by the defining relations of the input ring.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = skewPolynomialRing(QQ,(-1)_QQ,{w,x,y,z})  |
|                                                   |
|o1 = A                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : FreeAlgebraQuotient                           |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : x*y-y*x                                       |
|                                                   |
|o2 = -2y*x                                         |
|                                                   |
|o2 : A                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : w^2                                           |
|                                                   |
|      2                                            |
|o3 = w                                             |
|                                                   |
|o3 : A                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : B = toCommRing(A)                             |
|                                                   |
|o4 = B                                             |
|                                                   |
|o4 : QuotientRing                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : x*y                                           |
|                                                   |
|o5 = 0                                             |
|                                                   |
|o5 : B                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : w^2                                           |
|                                                   |
|      2                                            |
|o6 = w                                             |
|                                                   |
|o6 : B                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : C = toCommRing(A,SkewCommutative=>true)       |
|                                                   |
|o7 = C                                             |
|                                                   |
|o7 : PolynomialRing, 4 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : x*y-y*x                                       |
|                                                   |
|o8 = 2x*y                                          |
|                                                   |
|o8 : C                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : w^2                                           |
|                                                   |
|o9 = 0                                             |
|                                                   |
|o9 : C                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

