toFreeAlgebraQuotient -- Converts a Ring to a noncommutative ring
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        S = toFreeAlgebraQuotient R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * Outputs:
      * S, a *note quotient of a free algebra: FreeAlgebra / Ideal,, 

Description
===========

This function converts commutative rings and quotients of exterior algebras
(i.e. quotients of *note PolynomialRing: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,) to a
ring of type FreeAlgebraQuotient.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d, SkewCommutative=>{2,3}]                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 2 skew commutative variable(s)                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a*d-b*c)                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = ideal(- b*c + a*d)                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
